  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Clearing the way for development: Mine action in Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Clearing the way for development: Mine action in Libya - The proposed rapid response package will support UNSMIL in its multifaceted efforts to advance Libya&#xbf;s political process by providing financial support to the implementation of the political roadmap leading to national elections and the unification of Libya&#xbf;s political, administrative and economic institutions. The intense clashes that occurred between rival armed groups in Tripoli in May 2025 contaminated numerous neighbourhoods with unexploded ordnance (UXO).&amp;nbsp;This situation has led to a spike of injuries and impacted economic activities. The clearance of these urban areas has been recognised by the Libyan Mine Action Centre (LibMAC), the United Nations Mine Action Service (UNMAS) and UNSMIL as a priority. Hence, the EU will furthermore reinforce its support to a Libyan Mine Action NGO to engage in clearance of these UXO and to strengthen local rapid response capacity in mine action.</narrative>
  </description>
